cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If the ECA/DECA history, observable-contrast theory, implementation,
  experiments, or research archive contributes to your work, please cite this
  repository and the ISCAS 2025 ECA paper where appropriate.
type: software
title: >-
  Observable Contrast Research: From Eigen-Components to Additive and
  Symmetry-Resolved Physical Witnesses
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Rongzhou
    alias: Lachlan Chen
repository-code: "https://github.com/lachlanchen/discriminative-energy-component-analysis"
url: "https://github.com/lachlanchen/discriminative-energy-component-analysis"
version: 6.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-28
abstract: >-
  A reproducible research repository developing Eigen-Component Analysis into
  discriminative, additive, and symmetry-/subalgebra-accessible observable
  contrast. It includes exact binary and multiclass measurement formulations,
  mergeable streaming states, sequential evidence, symmetry-sector
  diagnostics, physical and chemical controlled experiments, Qiskit
  simulations, exact gauge-sector and accessible-process no-go benchmarks,
  cycle-fair syndrome-drift experiments, controlled surface-code decoder
  validation, a predeclared real-QEC syndrome benchmark with separated access
  phases and artifact provenance, historical sources, and six compiled
  working papers.
keywords:
  - eigen-component analysis
  - additive observable contrast
  - symmetry-resolved observable contrast
  - quantum state discrimination
  - positive operator-valued measure
  - trace distance
  - online change detection
  - invariant statistics
  - condensed matter physics
  - optical coherence
  - difference density
  - robotics
  - lattice gauge theory
  - topological order
  - Wilson loop
  - surface code
  - quantum error correction
  - real-device syndrome data
  - syndrome drift
  - sequential change detection
  - randomization inference
  - reproducible research
